Id: ssh028i
Severity: INFO
Category: ssh
Check: check_ssh
Fix: Set PrintLastLog yes (the default).
References: sshd_config(5); NIST SP 800-53 Rev. 5, AC-9 (Previous Logon Notification)
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST AC-9; ISO 8.5; CE Secure configuration

PrintLastLog is no: users are not told the date, time and origin of
their previous login when they log in interactively, so one of them who
did not make that login has no chance to notice it. The notice is cheap
and the default, and the control NIST calls previous logon notification
rests on it. Where the PAM stack shows the same through pam_lastlog it
is redundant, and a reason to accept this finding.
